course: dictionary
lesson: 12969
title: Official permission
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exemption is official permission not to do something that others must do. The word comes from exempt, which means let off or free from a duty. Often an exemption comes with a note, a form or a letter from someone in charge.
explain: «Ruby has an exemption from PE, with a note from her doctor.» Everyone else in her class must do PE, but Ruby has permission to sit it out. The clue is official permission: someone in charge has said yes.
explain: Exemption is also used about money. «This charity has a tax exemption, so it does not pay that tax.» A tax exemption means you do not have to pay a certain tax, even though most people do. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "This charity has official permission not to pay that tax" make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: An exemption is official permission not to do something that others must do.
fact: Exempt is the verb form: to be exempt from something means you do not have to do it.
fact: A tax exemption means you do not have to pay a certain tax.
fact: «Omar has an exemption from the uniform rule» can be allowed for religious reasons.
fact: Check the context: an exemption is usually given by someone in charge, such as a teacher, doctor or government.
exercise: «Ruby has an exemption from PE, with a note from her doctor.» What does exemption mean here? | A new kind of PE kit | *Official permission not to do PE | Extra lessons in PE | A sports prize
exercise: «This charity has a tax exemption, so it does not pay that tax.» What does tax exemption mean? | You can pay the tax later | *You do not have to pay that tax | You must pay double tax | You have to pay tax on everything
exercise: A notice says: «Pupils with a medical note may apply for an exemption.» What does apply for an exemption mean? | Pay a fine | Run to the office | *Ask for official permission not to do something | Wear a costume
test: Which is the best meaning of exemption? | A school trip | A type of food | *Official permission not to do something others must do | Being very loud
test: Tom has an exemption from swimming. What does he NOT have to do? | *Swim in the lessons | Wear a hat | Go to school | Bring a packed lunch
exam: Read: «Her exemption means she does not pay the tax.» What does exemption mean? | A large sum of money | A holiday from school | *Official permission not to pay something | A rule that everyone must follow
